"An Avowed can call on the System to emergency-teleport, or ET, themselves to safety."
"An ET works only if the Avowed is conscious to start it."
"Capsized Anesidoran boaters ET to the Teleportation Complex."
"Children cannot ET themselves, but authorities or parents can call one on their behalf."
"Avowed event security protects Avowed only until they have all ET'd out."
"Avowed ET'ing away while regular humans get hurt is a political nightmare."
"On Anesidora an ET draws on the island's shared teleport allotment, with an eight-second countdown."
"Allotment abusers go on a restricted list; ET is not for scrapes and bruises."
"A person may reject a teleport offered by others, but a preserved person can still be ET'd."
"An emergency teleport can be shared with another person."
